    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0319" n="1053" xml:id="pg1053"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. McKenzie.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Hicks’s No. 425, of
                    September 16, 1892, and previous correspondence in regard to the claim of the
                    Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon against Peru, the justice of which has
                    been acknowledged by the Peruvian Government, I inclose a copy of a
                        letter<anchor n="*" xml:id="d268-f1"/> from Mr. William Shands, executor of
                    one of the claimants, urging that the claim may be pressed to a conclusion.</p>
                <p>You will ascertain whether there is any prospect of obtaining its payment.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
